Description: DFA matching checks the size of a reused workspace block
 pcre2_dfa_match reused a cached workspace block for a recursive call
 without checking its size. A pattern that sets a low heap limit and
 recurses made the match write past the end of the block.
 Such a match now fails with a heap limit error. The size of a new
 block is also clamped to the heap limit without overflow.
 This is upstream's backport to 10.42 of c932e70451ea, the fix for
 GHSA-3r4p-g7gg-ppmf. The test data hunks add its regression test.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/PCRE2Project/pcre2/commit/26eb5f6712f2d2e6d3d012b273c53f7b4d420379
Bug: https://github.com/PCRE2Project/pcre2/security/advisories/GHSA-3r4p-g7gg-ppmf
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-17

--- a/src/pcre2_dfa_match.c
+++ b/src/pcre2_dfa_match.c
@@ -37,6 +37,8 @@
 POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGE.
